      "correct": "C",
      "answerText": "(C) Measures of location/position",
      "explanation": "Centiles (Percentiles), Deciles, and Quartiles are all measures of location or position (C). They are \"fractiles\" that divide a dataset, once it has been ordered from smallest to largest, into equal parts.\nCentiles divide the data into 100 equal parts. The 90th centile is the value below which 90% of the data falls.\nQuartiles divide the data into 4 equal parts. The 1st quartile (Q1) is the 25th centile, and the 3rd quartile (Q3) is the 75th centile.\nThey indicate the position of a particular value relative to the rest of the data. While the median (the 50th centile) is a measure of central tendency (A), and the interquartile range (Q3-Q1) is a measure of dispersion (B), the quartiles and centiles themselves are classified as measures of position.",
