      "explanation": "The Dependency Ratio is a demographic measure that shows the ratio of the non-working-age population (dependents) to the working-age population.\nDependents: This population consists of two groups:\n1. Young dependents (<15 years): 6000\n2. Old dependents (≥65 years): 2000\n3. Total Dependents = 6000 + 2000 = 8000\nWorking-age Population: This is the population aged 15-64 years.\nWorking-age Population = 12000\nDependency Ratio Calculation:\nDependency Ratio = (Total Dependents / Working-age Population) × 100%\nDependency Ratio = (8000 / 12000) × 100%\nDependency Ratio = (8 / 12) × 100%\nDependency Ratio = (2 / 3) × 100% = 0.666... × 100% = 66.6...%\nThe closest answer is 66% (C).",
