      "explanation": "Triage is the process of prioritizing patients based on the severity of their condition, especially in mass casualty incidents or busy emergency departments. A color-coded system is commonly used.\n1. Red (Priority 1) : Indicates patients with immediate, life-threatening injuries (e.g., airway obstruction, severe bleeding, shock) who have a high chance of survival if they receive immediate medical intervention.\n2. Yellow (Priority 2) : For patients with serious injuries that are not immediately life-threatening but require urgent care (e.g., major fractures, open wounds).\n3. Green (Priority 3) : The \"walking wounded\"; patients with minor injuries who can wait for treatment (e.g., minor cuts, sprains).\n4. Black (Priority 0) : For patients who are deceased or have injuries so severe that they are unlikely to survive even with medical care.\nTherefore, patients requiring immediate life-threatening care are tagged as Red.",
