      "statement": "A 5-year-old child develops facial swelling that becomes generalized with pedal edema and ascites. He responds well to steroids. His RBS is 112 mg/dL, urine tests are normal, and kidney biopsy electron microscopy shows podocyte effacement. What is the most likely diagnosis?",
