      "explanation": "The detection of abnormal gene sequences involves various molecular biology techniques. Restriction Fragment Length Polymorphism (RFLP) analysis  is a classic technique that can detect sequence variations that alter restriction enzyme cutting sites. Porcelainizing  is a method of DNA sequencing that can identify the exact nucleotide sequence of a gene. Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization (FISH)  uses fluorescent probes to detect the presence, absence, or location of specific DNA sequences on chromosomes, and is used for detecting larger scale abnormalities like deletions or translocations. In contrast, flow cytometry  is a technique used to analyze the physical and chemical characteristics of cells. It is primarily used to measure cell surface protein expression (immunophenotyping), cell size, and granularity, and for cell sorting. It analyzes proteins on the cell surface, not the underlying gene sequence.",
