      "statement": "A pregnant woman at 30 weeks presents with painful vaginal bleeding and decreased fetal movements. Examination shows a tense uterus measuring 34 weeks, absent fetal heart rate, BP 160/90, and on vaginal exam the cervix is 6 cm dilated, 70% effaced, with a vertex at –3 and intact membranes. What is the most appropriate immediate step?",
