      "number": 386,
      "printedNumber": 187,
      "paperSession": "Nov 2023",
      "statement": "Mark the correct statement/statements regarding Inner and Outer hair cells? I. Inner hair cells are in a single row and transmit auditory impulses. II. Outer hair cells are in 3-4 rows and modulate function of inner hair cells. III. Outer hair cells are more responsible for movement of Tectorial membrane. IV. Outer and inner hair cells present in the ratio of 3:1.",
      "options": [
        "I, II and IV are correct",
        "I, II and III are correct",
        "All are correct",
        "II, IV are correct"
      ],
      "correct": "A",
      "answerText": "(A) I, II and IV are correct",
      "explanation": "1. Statement I is correct. Inner hair cells (IHCs) are arranged in a single row along the cochlea and are the primary sensory receptors of hearing. They convert mechanical sound vibrations into electrical impulses and transmit auditory signals through the cochlear nerve to the brain.\n2. Statement II is also correct. Outer hair cells (OHCs) are arranged in three to four rows and function mainly as modulators. They possess electromotility due to the motor protein prestin, allowing them to contract and elongate. This action amplifies basilar membrane vibrations and enhances the sensitivity and frequency selectivity of inner hair cells.\n3. Statement III is incorrect. The primary movement of the tectorial membrane results from sound-induced vibration of the basilar membrane. Outer hair cells mainly amplify and fine-tune this motion rather than being directly responsible for moving the tectorial membrane.\n4. Statement IV is correct. Outer hair cells outnumber inner hair cells in approximately a 3:1 ratio.\nTherefore, statements I, II, and IV are correct.",
      "pages": [
        321,
        370
      ],
