      "statement": "A 52-year-old woman comes for her routine screening mammogram, which shows a few scattered punctate calcifications in both breasts that are unchanged from her study two years ago. She takes atorvastatin and a daily vitamin. She is worried about these findings. What BI-RADS category should she receive, and how should these results be explained to her?",
