      "correct": "A",
      "answerText": "(A) Eating disorder",
      "explanation": "The SCOFF questionnaire is a brief and widely used screening tool designed to help identify individuals who may have an eating disorder, such as anorexia nervosa or bulimia nervosa. It is a simple, five-question instrument that is easy to remember due to its acronym, SCOFF. The five questions are:\n1. Do you make yourself Sick because you feel uncomfortably full?\n2. Do you worry you have lost Control over how much you eat?\n3. Have you recently lost more than One stone (14 lbs or 6.35 kg) in a three-month period?\n4. Do you believe yourself to be Fat when others say you are too thin?\n5. Would you say that Food dominates your life?\nA score of two or more positive answers suggests a high likelihood of an underlying eating disorder and warrants a more detailed clinical evaluation.",
