      "explanation": "A disinfectant is a chemical that destroys or irreversibly inactivates most pathogenic microorganisms on inanimate surfaces. A sanitizer reduces microbial contamination to a safe level but does not eliminate all pathogens. Bleaching powder (calcium hypochlorite) is a powerful oxidizing agent that releases chlorine. It is a broad-spectrum, high-level disinfectant used for surfaces and water treatment, capable of killing bacteria, viruses, and fungi. Hydrogen peroxide (A) can act as a disinfectant at high concentrations (>3%) but is used as an antiseptic at lower concentrations. Penicillin (B) is an antibiotic for therapeutic use inside the body. Methyl paraben (C) is primarily a preservative used to inhibit microbial growth in products like cosmetics and foods; it is bacteriostatic/fungistatic, not a disinfectant. Bleaching powder's primary role is disinfection.",
