      "explanation": "According to the National Blindness and Visual Impairment Survey (India, 2015–2019), untreated cataract was reported as the most common cause of moderate to severe visual impairment (MSVI) as well as blindness in adults aged 50 years and above.\nWhile uncorrected refractive error is a major contributor to visual impairment globally, the Indian national survey data specifically identified untreated cataract as the leading cause of MSVI in the surveyed population. Cataract causes progressive clouding of the lens, leading to gradual reduction in visual acuity. Because many affected individuals do not undergo timely cataract surgery, it remains the most significant cause.\nRefractive errors were reported as the second most common cause of visual impairment. Glaucoma and diabetic retinopathy contribute smaller proportions compared to cataract.\nThus, based on the National Blindness and Visual Impairment Survey (2015–2019), the most common cause of moderate to severe visual impairment is : (B) Untreated cataract",
