      "paperSession": "Nov 2022",
      "statement": "A 27-year-old woman presents with sudden vision loss in her right eye along with a relative afferent pupillary defect (RAPD), while the left eye appears normal. Which investigation should be performed next? 1 MRI of the brain and orbits, testing for Myelin Oligodendrocyte Glycoprotein (MOG) and Neuromyelitis Optica (NMO) antibodies, and Blood Sugar levels 2 MRI of the brain and orbits, and testing for Myelin Oligodendrocyte Glycoprotein (MOG) and Neuromyelitis Optica (NMO) antibodies 3 Testing for Myelin Oligodendrocyte Glycoprotein (MOG) and Neuromyelitis Optica (NMO) antibodies, and Blood Sugar levels 4 Blood Sugar levels and Thyroid profile",
