      "paperSession": "May 2022",
      "statement": "A 65-year-old woman weighing 60 kg is on mechanical ventilation for ARDS due to urosepsis. Her ventilator settings are: tidal volume 360 mL, respiratory rate 30/min, PEEP 5 cm H₂O, and FiO₂ 90%. Arterial blood gas results show PaO₂ 50 mmHg, PaCO₂ 38 mmHg, and pH 7.38. What should be the next adjustment to her ventilatory management?",
