      "correct": "C",
      "answerText": "(C) Stage of compensatory shock is also called stage 2 of shock",
      "explanation": "Shock is commonly divided into stages:\n1. Initial stage (Stage 1) – Early cellular hypoxia begins; anaerobic metabolism starts.\n2. Compensatory stage (Stage 2) – The body activates compensatory mechanisms such as tachycardia, peripheral vasoconstriction, and activation of the renin–angiotensin–aldosterone system to maintain blood pressure and perfusion.\n3. Progressive stage (Stage 3) – Worsening tissue hypoxia and metabolic acidosis.\n4. Irreversible stage (Stage 4) – Multi-organ failure and death.\nNow reviewing other options:\n1. (A) is false because anaerobic respiration produces lactic acid, not carbon dioxide.\n2. (B) is incorrect in general classification; hypovolemic shock is often cited as the most common overall, though septic shock is the most common distributive type.\n3. (D) is false because anaphylactic shock is due to a Type I (IgE-mediated) hypersensitivity reaction, not Type II.\nThus, the correct statement is (C).",
