      "statement": "A 32-year-old man arrives at the surgical emergency department with a 2-day history of abdominal pain, bloating, and constipation suggestive of peptic ulcer disease. An X-ray image is provided. Which combination of management steps is most appropriate for this patient?\n1. IV fluids\n2. CECT (Contrast-Enhanced Computed Tomography) of the abdomen\n3. Exploratory laparotomy\n4. Upper Gl (gastrointestinal) endoscopy Below is the provided x-ray film image.",
