      "paperSession": "Nov 2021",
      "statement": "Which one of the following is not a component of meta-analysis?",
      "options": [
        "Selection",
        "Analysis",
        "Randomization",
        "Abstraction"
      ],
      "correct": "C",
      "answerText": "(C) Randomization",
      "explanation": "A meta-analysis is a statistical method used to combine the results of multiple independent studies to derive a single, more powerful conclusion. The process involves several key steps :\n1. Selection : Defining clear inclusion and exclusion criteria to select the relevant studies for the analysis.\n2. Abstraction : Systematically extracting the relevant data (e.g., sample size, effect estimates, standard errors) from each selected study.\n3. Analysis : Using statistical techniques to pool the data and calculate an overall summary effect measure.\n4. Randomization, however, is a component of the design of the primary studies being analyzed (specifically, randomized controlled trials). It is not a component of the meta-analysis process itself. A meta-analysis analyzes studies that may or may not have used randomization; it does not perform randomization.",
