      "paperSession": "May 2021",
      "statement": "A 50-year-old man arrives with sudden onset of right-sided weakness and aphasia within the past two hours. His blood pressure is 160/110 mmHg, and his non-contrast CT (NCCT) head scan shows no abnormalities. What should be the next step in his management?",
