      "statement": "A 68-year-old man with hypertension, diabetes, and coronary artery disease presents with palpitations and shortness of breath. His heartbeat is irregular, and ECG shows an irregular rhythm with no P waves and no isoelectric baseline. His vitals are BP 132/84 mmHg, HR 130 bpm, and SpO₂ 94% on room air. Based on these findings, which treatment should be considered the first-line option for this patient?",
