      "statement": "A 45-year-old patient presents to the emergency department with severe pain in a casted tibia fracture. After removing the cast, the examination shows painful passive extension, intact dorsalis pedis and posterior tibial pulses, and loss of sensation over the first web space. What is the most appropriate next step in managing this patient?",
