      "explanation": "Lower urinary tract symptoms (LUTS) refer to symptoms arising from the bladder, urethra, or prostate and are classified into storage, voiding, and post-micturition symptoms. Storage symptoms include urgency, frequency, nocturia, and urinary incontinence. (A)\tOption, sudden urge to urinate, represents urgency and is a classic storage symptom of LUTS. (B)\tOption, incontinence while asleep, corresponds to nocturnal enuresis and is also categorized under storage LUTS. (C)\tOption, incontinence when the patient lies down and coughs, describes stress urinary incontinence, which occurs due to increased intra-abdominal pressure and is included among lower urinary tract symptoms. (D)\tOption, incontinence during intercourse, is termed coital incontinence. Although it involves urinary leakage, it is generally considered part of sexual dysfunction rather than being classified within the standard LUTS framework. It is not routinely included in the International Continence Society’s core LUTS classification. Therefore, the correct answer is (D) Incontinence during intercourse.",
