      "correct": "C",
      "answerText": "(C) 30-300 Seconds",
      "explanation": "Short-term memory (STM) refers to the temporary storage of information for a brief period before it is either forgotten or consolidated into long-term memory. It typically lasts from about 30 seconds to 5 minutes (300 seconds) in the absence of rehearsal.\nShort-term memory has a limited capacity, often described by Miller’s law as 7 ± 2 items, although more recent research suggests it may be closer to 4–7 items. Information in short-term memory can be maintained longer through active rehearsal (repeating the information mentally).\nIn contrast :\n1. Sensory memory lasts only a few seconds (about 1–3 seconds).\n2. Working memory is closely related to short-term memory but includes active processing.\n3. Long-term memory can last from hours to a lifetime.\nThus, the typical duration of short-term memory is 30–300 seconds, making option (C) correct.",
