      "paperSession": "Nov 2020",
      "statement": "A road-traffic-accident (RTA) patient with polytrauma has unstable vitals, is intubated due to a low Glasgow Coma Scale (GCS), shows no eye opening, no verbal response, no motor response to pain, and CT scan reveals brain edema. What is the most likely cause?",
