      "explanation": "The European Hernia Society (EHS) classification system is a standardized method for classifying primary and incisional ventral hernias. The classification is based on the location and size of the hernia defect. For midline hernias, the letter 'M' is used. The location is further specified by a number corresponding to a specific zone :\n1. M1 : Subxiphoid\n2. M2 : Epigastric\n3. M3 : Umbilical\n4. M4 : Infraumbilical\n5. M5 : Suprapubic\nThe width of the defect is then classified as W1 (<2 cm), W2 (2-4 cm), or W3 (>4 cm). Therefore, an M3 hernia specifically refers to a hernia located in the umbilical region.",
