      "explanation": "This question assesses the basic life support (BLS) algorithm for an unresponsive adult. The correct sequence of actions for a single rescuer is :\n1. Check for safety of the scene.\n2. Check for responsiveness (tap and shout).\n3. If unresponsive, immediately shout for nearby help and activate the emergency response system (e.g., call the local emergency number). If you are alone, you can do this with a mobile phone on speaker.\n4. Simultaneously, check for breathing and a carotid pulse for no more than 10 seconds.\n5. If there is no pulse or no normal breathing, immediately begin high-quality CPR, starting with chest compressions.\nOption (B) follows this correct sequence : activating help first, then assessing the patient, and then initiating CPR. Option (A) incorrectly prioritizes starting CPR before calling for help, which would delay the arrival of advanced medical care and a defibrillator.",
